window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>What if the person you loved… wasn’t entirely in control of herself? And the voice inside her head wasn’t her own?</p> <p>Nathan Longton enjoys a quiet life running a café in Preston until Lan Nguyen, a beautiful, panicked student, stumbles into his world. She’s being followed, haunted by a voice she can’t explain… and wearing a necklace identical to Nathan’s.</p> <p>Their connection is no coincidence.</p> <p>With help from Ollie, his sarcastic, tech-savvy best friend, and Marcus, a jaded ex-scientist with a knack for cutting through the madness (and everyone’s patience), Nathan begins to uncover the truth: Project Janus Origin, a secretive experiment in mind control, memory manipulation, and human identity.</p> <p>As the voice in Lan’s head grows more controlling and the danger deepens, Nathan is forced to question everything: Is their bond genuine… or engineered?</p> <p>And when your thoughts are no longer your own, can your heart still be trusted?</p> <p>Blending slow-burn psychological suspense, sharp humour, romance, and sci-fi intrigue. <i>Janus Origin: Thread of Control</i> is perfect for listeners who enjoy the speculative bite of <i>Black Mirror</i>, the pace of <i>The Atlantis Gene</i>, the wit of Matt Haig, and the sly suspense of Mick Herron. An offbeat romantic thriller where nothing is as it seems, threaded with humour and a mind-bending twist.</p>"; 
